From f39a67343bf28cc486adf8d211d5e6c0abba0399 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:01:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Client: ESBT is the engine; Loro and Yjs engines removed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EsbtEngine keeps the loro-engine shape — IndexedDB warm open behind a
persist lock, network-aware shallow HTTP snapshot, one WebSocket with a
version vector on the URL, reconnect backoff, deletion close code,
cross-tab BroadcastChannel sync, hydration state — on the @marks/esbt
replica, with per-peer undo grouped over a 500 ms window and comment
writes excluded from Mod-Z by origin. Comments ride the engine's keyed
LWW map with weight-stable anchors standing in for Loro Cursors; the
shared quote resolver stays as the fallback. Remote carets and
selections move to a new presence extension (collab/presence.ts) that
publishes the contract's ${siteId}-cm-user / ${siteId}-cm-sel keys on a
15 s heartbeat and renders peers as CodeMirror decorations, replacing
loro-codemirror and y-codemirror.next. Single-engine UI (no engine
picker), legacy loro/yjs rows are listed but refused with an
explanation, and the benchmark page now measures ESBT. loro-crdt,
loro-codemirror, yjs, y-codemirror.next, y-indexeddb and
@hocuspocus/provider leave the dependency tree.
